      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we first need to calculate the volumes of both the original pyramid and the smaller pyramid that is cut off from the top.\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the original pyramid:**\n   The formula for the volume of a pyramid is given by:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{Base Area} \\times \\text{Height}\n   \\]\n   For the original pyramid, the base is a square with edge length 12 cm, so the base area is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Base Area} = 12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   The height of the original pyramid is 8 cm. Therefore, the volume of the original pyramid is:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid:**\n   For the smaller pyramid, the base is a square with edge length 6 cm, so the base area is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Base Area} = 6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   The height of the smaller pyramid is 4 cm. Therefore, the volume of the smaller pyramid is:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the volume of the frustum:**\n   The volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{small}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{336}\\) cubic centimeters.",
