      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the volume of the frustum, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the original pyramid.**\n2. **Calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid.**\n3. **Subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the original pyramid to find the volume of the frustum.**\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the volume of the original pyramid\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a pyramid is given by:\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{Base Area} \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nFor the original pyramid:\n- The base edge is 12 cm.\n- The altitude (height) is 8 cm.\n\nFirst, calculate the area of the base (which is a square):\n\\[ \\text{Base Area} = 12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\n\nNow, calculate the volume of the original pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid\n\nFor the smaller pyramid:\n- The base edge is 6 cm.\n- The altitude (height) is 4 cm.\n\nFirst, calculate the area of the base (which is also a square):\n\\[ \\text{Base Area} = 6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\n\nNow, calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{smaller}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the volume of the frustum\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the difference between the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{smaller}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThus, the volume of the frustum is:\n\\[ \\boxed{336} \\]",
