      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we need to calculate the volume of the entire original pyramid and subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid.\n\nThe volume \\(V\\) of a pyramid is given by the formula:\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{Base Area} \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the volume of the original pyramid:\nThe base edge of the original pyramid is 12 cm and the height (altitude) is 8 cm.\nThe area of the base (square of the base edge) is:\n\\[ \\text{Base Area} = 12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\nSo, the volume of the original pyramid is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid:\nThe base edge of the smaller pyramid is 6 cm and the height is 4 cm.\nThe area of the base (square of the base edge) is:\n\\[ \\text{Base Area} = 6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\nSo, the volume of the smaller pyramid is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{small}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the frustum is:\n\\[ \\boxed{336} \\]",
